WEBVTT

00:08.174 --> 00:10.343
Mr. Sakamoto! Stop, please!

00:12.220 --> 00:13.804
Why are you doing this to me?!

00:13.805 --> 00:15.305
- Mr. Sakamoto!
- I'll hold him down.

00:15.306 --> 00:18.392
- I'll work harder! I'll get stronger!
- Do it before he wriggles away.

00:18.393 --> 00:20.353
Please, I'm begging you!

00:25.483 --> 00:27.609
<i>-After the fight with Saw...</i>
- I'm gonna die!

00:27.610 --> 00:30.362
<i>...Mr. Sakamoto took us
to his physical therapist.</i>

00:30.363 --> 00:32.031
Help me, Mr. Sakamoto!

00:32.032 --> 00:35.534
Quit bein' a baby.
It's just a little acupuncture.

00:35.535 --> 00:38.955
MIYA CLINIC
PHYSICAL THERAPY - ACUPUNCTURE

02:10.046 --> 02:13.590
STRONG ASSAULT

02:13.591 --> 02:14.675
GRANNY MIYA
THERAPIST

02:14.676 --> 02:16.468
I barely recognized you.

02:16.469 --> 02:19.764
I don't have any customers as fat as you.

02:20.390 --> 02:25.269
And I don't remember
advertising for ex-hit men, either.

02:25.270 --> 02:27.020
You're the only one who can heal that.

02:27.021 --> 02:29.731
Hey, don't mess with them, you dumbass!

02:29.732 --> 02:30.858
Mr. Sakamoto, Lu's...

02:30.859 --> 02:32.527
Doesn't it hurt?

02:33.653 --> 02:36.322
Actually, it feels surprisingly good.

02:36.948 --> 02:39.117
That old lady really knows
what she's doing.

02:40.493 --> 02:44.621
Granny Miya is famous among hit men
for her amazing healing techniques.

02:44.622 --> 02:45.874
Really?

02:46.541 --> 02:50.502
<i>She's known as the Hand of God
throughout the underworld.</i>

02:50.503 --> 02:55.466
<i>She can heal almost any wound,
even ones from the deadliest battles.</i>

02:56.175 --> 02:57.342
Wow.

02:57.343 --> 02:59.219
Long as you ain't dead.

02:59.220 --> 03:01.389
Old lady, how long do I have to do this?

03:02.015 --> 03:03.932
Rude little brat, ain'tcha.

03:03.933 --> 03:06.102
I'm still only 98, ya know.

03:06.728 --> 03:09.104
Keep 'em in
at least for the rest of the day.

03:09.105 --> 03:10.440
What?!

03:11.357 --> 03:14.193
Using that new ability of yours

03:14.903 --> 03:18.489
<i>is like sprinting at full speed
while holding your breath.</i>

03:19.324 --> 03:21.408
At this point,

03:21.409 --> 03:24.244
I'd say you can handle
five minutes a day, tops.

03:24.245 --> 03:26.122
Five minutes?! That's it?

03:26.789 --> 03:28.750
Do what you want. It's your funeral.

03:29.459 --> 03:32.503
Granny, could you see to me too?

03:33.254 --> 03:36.089
I feel kinda dizzy.

03:36.090 --> 03:37.008
Lemme see.

03:38.092 --> 03:41.303
Ah, I see. That's no good.

03:41.304 --> 03:43.430
You've got toxins built up in your body.

03:43.431 --> 03:44.932
MISO SOUP
FRESHWATER CLAMS

03:44.933 --> 03:47.894
Drink this. Miso soup with clams.

03:52.065 --> 03:53.523
I feel better already!

03:53.524 --> 03:55.192
You just had a hangover!

03:55.193 --> 03:56.526
- Want some, Shin?
- Taro.

03:56.527 --> 03:57.444
Oh, that's good.

03:57.445 --> 03:59.280
Your turn.

03:59.948 --> 04:02.367
It's been a while.
Let Granny give you a checkup.

04:05.536 --> 04:10.375
Gotta say, I never thought
I'd see you working as part of a team.

04:10.959 --> 04:12.669
Those kiddos seem nice.

04:14.671 --> 04:18.091
You're fixing to go bust some skulls
after this, aren't you?

04:18.925 --> 04:20.092
Why do you ask?

04:20.093 --> 04:22.845
This is the pressure point for anger.

04:23.429 --> 04:25.640
It only hurts if you're angry.

04:26.266 --> 04:28.600
Don't think you can hide anything from me.

04:28.601 --> 04:30.812
It doesn't hurt one bit.

04:31.437 --> 04:32.562
<i>It hurts so bad...</i>

04:32.563 --> 04:36.900
Those kids getting attacked...
Well, that'd send anyone into a rage.

04:36.901 --> 04:39.904
But no good'll come of you
rushing into things on your own.

04:41.072 --> 04:44.449
Just so you know, you're only at about...

04:44.450 --> 04:48.413
I'd say 30% of how strong you were
back in your prime.

04:49.038 --> 04:52.959
The five-year break has put
a big gap between you and Nacchan.

04:54.002 --> 04:56.254
<i>In case you're wondering,
they put me at rank S.</i>

05:02.093 --> 05:03.219
It doesn't matter.

05:03.720 --> 05:05.887
I'm not going to let them
hurt anyone else.

05:05.888 --> 05:07.098
Wait a second.

05:10.018 --> 05:12.728
That was the pressure point
called the <i>seika tanden.</i>

05:12.729 --> 05:14.939
It should do you some good.

05:16.274 --> 05:18.151
Thanks, Granny Miya.

05:19.193 --> 05:20.569
Take care of those two for me.

05:20.570 --> 05:22.070
Come back here! Lemme try!

05:22.071 --> 05:24.531
- It's an ancient method!
- Good luck. You'll need it.

05:24.532 --> 05:27.326
Liar! Get away from me,
you drunken kung-fu freak!

05:27.327 --> 05:30.079
SAKAMOTO'S

05:34.959 --> 05:36.961
Can I help you find something?

05:38.463 --> 05:40.339
Where is Taro Sakamoto?

05:40.965 --> 05:44.218
My husband's not here right now.
He went to his physical therapist.

05:45.011 --> 05:46.721
Don't try to hide him from me.

05:47.680 --> 05:50.432
I hate being lied to.

05:50.433 --> 05:53.351
What? I hate lies too...

05:53.352 --> 05:56.189
I don't think you understand
your situation here.

06:07.992 --> 06:09.786
What happens to the money inside?

06:20.004 --> 06:21.255
Hello.

06:23.382 --> 06:25.510
Do you understand now?

06:26.594 --> 06:28.596
Where is Taro Sakamoto?

06:29.388 --> 06:31.765
Try to hide him and I'll crush you next.

06:31.766 --> 06:33.267
Now, be a good girl and--

06:41.150 --> 06:43.527
What the... Who are you?

06:43.528 --> 06:46.863
Oh, dear. What a mess you've made.

06:46.864 --> 06:49.533
I bet that's what she'd say. Oh?

06:49.534 --> 06:52.202
I was wondering why you were still alive.

06:52.203 --> 06:54.663
Looks like this was a toy knife.

06:54.664 --> 06:59.584
<i>This is the guy from the list... The S-rank.</i>

06:59.585 --> 07:02.838
I'm gonna kill you. I hate liars.

07:02.839 --> 07:04.423
Not a chance.

07:08.010 --> 07:11.431
You see, I'm on the clock right now.

07:12.515 --> 07:15.684
Nagumo, watch the store while I'm out.

07:15.685 --> 07:17.352
I'm worried about Aoi and Hana.

07:17.353 --> 07:19.855
What? I don't wanna.

07:19.856 --> 07:22.650
You owe me, remember?

07:23.568 --> 07:25.986
You could've asked nicely, at least.

07:25.987 --> 07:28.280
You better pay me.

07:28.281 --> 07:29.198
Sure.

07:30.950 --> 07:34.537
Gotta help your friends out, you know?

07:37.165 --> 07:39.125
Look, Piisuke!

07:39.792 --> 07:42.878
This is crazy! The floor is see-through!

07:42.879 --> 07:44.672
So scary...

07:45.339 --> 07:48.885
I know! I'm not just fooling around here.

07:49.469 --> 07:51.762
It's like my grandma always said.

07:52.305 --> 07:54.389
When you can't find something
anywhere you look,

07:54.390 --> 07:57.393
it's probably right under your nose.

08:02.440 --> 08:05.568
I need to get to know even more people.

08:06.652 --> 08:09.197
Everybody... I want to know about everybody.

08:10.448 --> 08:11.449
Hey.

08:12.158 --> 08:13.576
What are you thinking about?

08:14.827 --> 08:16.786
What are you thinking about right now?

08:16.787 --> 08:19.916
What the hell? What do you want?

08:20.500 --> 08:22.835
Show me what's on the inside.

08:24.212 --> 08:26.671
We found him, Piisuke!

08:26.672 --> 08:29.132
Grandma was right after all.

08:29.133 --> 08:30.968
Her advice is always dead-on!

08:39.310 --> 08:40.311
What?

08:41.229 --> 08:44.981
He stopped the bullet! Just like Taro did.

08:44.982 --> 08:47.818
Wait... How much will it cost
to fix the glass?!

08:56.244 --> 08:58.371
So scary!

09:01.749 --> 09:03.417
What's his deal?

09:05.211 --> 09:06.712
Thanks, Piisuke!

09:15.388 --> 09:17.556
You see, I like string.

09:17.557 --> 09:22.812
We're all connected to each other
by invisible strings, aren't we?

09:27.650 --> 09:28.943
Oh, no!

09:29.569 --> 09:30.611
It's strange...

09:31.195 --> 09:36.993
Somehow, I have a feeling
that you're beautiful on the inside.

09:41.080 --> 09:43.415
That was close.

09:43.416 --> 09:44.499
What?

09:44.500 --> 09:47.503
I'm lucky he just happened to be nearby!

10:00.057 --> 10:02.809
Sorry, Heisuke.
Didn't mean to make you wait.

10:02.810 --> 10:04.686
No worries! You saved me!

10:04.687 --> 10:09.358
<i>I knew you'd be able
to figure out my clue, Taro!</i>

10:11.611 --> 10:12.945
That hurt...

10:14.155 --> 10:16.157
It's been forever...

10:16.741 --> 10:18.326
since I've been hit like that.

10:18.868 --> 10:21.704
Someone who can punch that hard

10:22.413 --> 10:24.457
might just be able

10:25.333 --> 10:27.501
to understand me.

10:29.086 --> 10:30.504
I'll take care of this one.

10:31.881 --> 10:34.383
For some reason,
I'm feeling pretty good today.

10:44.644 --> 10:47.146
432 people.

10:47.688 --> 10:52.318
I've killed 432 people,
but it hasn't satisfied my boredom.

10:52.943 --> 10:56.404
I wonder if killing you will change that?

10:56.405 --> 10:58.907
You count the number
of people you've killed?

10:58.908 --> 11:00.409
Surprisingly detail-oriented.

11:05.122 --> 11:07.457
Try not to break too much stuff.

11:07.458 --> 11:10.044
Or I'll get an earful from Sakamoto.

11:10.628 --> 11:12.003
What are you doing?

11:12.004 --> 11:13.421
Just borrowing your phone.

11:13.422 --> 11:16.217
You don't have Slur's number?

11:16.759 --> 11:17.927
Nor many friends, huh?

11:18.552 --> 11:21.221
<i>My phone... When did he take it?</i>

11:21.222 --> 11:24.100
You were so open, I couldn't help myself.

11:24.683 --> 11:26.310
Let's peek at your search history!

11:27.269 --> 11:29.020
Don't mess with me.

11:29.021 --> 11:30.689
Give it back!

11:33.275 --> 11:35.693
Sorry, are you sensitive
to all that privacy stuff?

11:35.694 --> 11:37.571
You slippery little...

11:43.619 --> 11:46.789
I wonder if there's more alien poop today!

11:47.540 --> 11:49.542
They must be having a party.

11:52.711 --> 11:54.338
<i>Where is he?</i>

11:54.922 --> 11:56.131
<i>How'd he disappear?</i>

11:56.132 --> 11:57.550
<i>Did he run away?</i>

11:58.092 --> 12:00.719
<i>No. His bag is here.</i>

12:01.595 --> 12:02.888
<i>He must be hiding.</i>

12:03.806 --> 12:04.974
Come out!

12:05.558 --> 12:06.891
Where are you?!

12:06.892 --> 12:09.019
Come out and fight me!

12:09.562 --> 12:12.231
Come on, you coward!

12:25.744 --> 12:27.121
Ta-da, it's me!

12:28.372 --> 12:32.292
<i>He's so small... How can he be this strong?</i>

12:32.293 --> 12:34.336
Let's see...

12:36.172 --> 12:41.134
Gum, a car key, a receipt for <i>gyudon,</i>

12:41.135 --> 12:43.179
and this hit list.

12:43.762 --> 12:46.097
You don't have any actual info, do you?

12:46.098 --> 12:47.808
Just a bunch of trash.

12:48.309 --> 12:49.685
I'm done.

12:51.479 --> 12:54.732
Now, since I'm such a nice guy,

12:55.232 --> 12:59.612
I'll let you choose how you die.

13:00.237 --> 13:02.656
<i>What's that? Some kind of weapon?</i>

13:05.951 --> 13:07.786
How do you wanna go out?

13:08.746 --> 13:11.873
This thing has six different functions.

13:11.874 --> 13:14.335
I gotta say, it's super handy.

13:15.085 --> 13:19.798
It'd be so boring
if I had to kill the same way every time.

13:21.634 --> 13:25.554
Come on. Pick a number, one to six.

13:26.138 --> 13:29.391
Screw you! Don't you dare belittle me!

13:29.975 --> 13:33.437
I'll crush you into nothing
just like I always do!

13:34.021 --> 13:35.939
What, you're not gonna choose?

13:35.940 --> 13:38.025
Fine, we'll let this decide.

13:42.196 --> 13:43.697
Where'd it go?

13:47.743 --> 13:48.994
Three, huh?

13:49.912 --> 13:52.164
How unfortunate.

13:57.336 --> 14:00.381
Number three is a giant can opener.

14:01.131 --> 14:02.508
But I guess you're not listening.

14:03.801 --> 14:05.970
Did we make too much of a mess?

14:06.512 --> 14:10.432
Man, Sakamoto's gonna kill me.

14:18.357 --> 14:20.025
EMERGENCY EXIT

14:22.486 --> 14:24.195
Strange.

14:24.196 --> 14:27.115
He's so fat, but he can move well.

14:27.116 --> 14:28.367
Taro!

14:33.789 --> 14:34.748
What?

14:35.291 --> 14:37.251
I can't seem to lose the weight.

14:40.462 --> 14:42.548
<i>What did she do to me?</i>

14:50.723 --> 14:51.599
You okay?!

14:52.850 --> 14:55.184
Hmm, it's not cutting through.

14:55.185 --> 14:57.021
You must be pretty sturdy.

14:57.897 --> 14:59.063
Taro!

14:59.064 --> 15:00.190
<i>Hot...</i>

15:03.444 --> 15:04.862
Did it work?

15:08.449 --> 15:10.700
He's like a spider!

15:10.701 --> 15:12.619
<i>He's skillful, for sure.</i>

15:12.620 --> 15:14.871
What have you done?!

15:14.872 --> 15:16.789
This is terrible!

15:16.790 --> 15:17.790
MODEL KITS

15:17.791 --> 15:20.336
They were arranged so neatly!

15:20.878 --> 15:23.046
Not sure what his deal is,
but this is my chance.

15:23.047 --> 15:25.298
- Why'd you do this?!
- While he's busy cleaning up,

15:25.299 --> 15:26.634
I'm going to slim down.

15:32.890 --> 15:34.807
Woah, look at you go!

15:34.808 --> 15:36.602
How's that?

15:39.146 --> 15:40.898
Why isn't it working?

15:45.986 --> 15:47.236
<i>Damn him.</i>

15:47.237 --> 15:48.322
Oh, no!

15:51.492 --> 15:53.326
<i>That string is sharp.</i>

15:53.327 --> 15:55.120
<i>I can't do this barehanded, but...</i>

15:58.207 --> 15:59.208
I have no weapons.

16:00.250 --> 16:01.793
Disgusting...

16:01.794 --> 16:04.545
Look at how dirty your pockets are!

16:04.546 --> 16:07.174
I don't think we'll be able
to understand each other.

16:07.758 --> 16:11.011
<i>But oddly enough, my body feels good.</i>

16:12.179 --> 16:16.099
Mr. Sakamoto is only at 30% strength
compared to his prime?!

16:16.100 --> 16:19.644
At least when he's that big.

16:19.645 --> 16:21.270
That's hard to believe.

16:21.271 --> 16:23.481
Do you think his body feels heavy?

16:23.482 --> 16:25.442
I'm sure that's part of it, but...

16:25.943 --> 16:32.115
Well, people who come back after a break
always try to move like they used to.

16:32.116 --> 16:34.535
If he just slims down,
that's not a problem, is it?

16:35.953 --> 16:37.870
If you ask me,

16:37.871 --> 16:42.041
he should learn the right way to move
with his new body weight.

16:42.042 --> 16:43.127
Huh?

16:43.877 --> 16:47.463
This whole time, I've been thinking.

16:47.464 --> 16:48.965
You're so sloppy.

16:48.966 --> 16:49.883
What?

16:50.467 --> 16:54.053
I don't get along well
with people like you.

16:54.054 --> 16:57.975
People who don't take good care of things
can't take good care of people, either.

16:58.559 --> 17:03.479
That's why you have no problem
walking all over guys like me.

17:03.480 --> 17:06.649
I'm not a sloppy person... I don't think.

17:06.650 --> 17:09.193
You sure about that?
Just look at your slippers.

17:09.194 --> 17:10.570
What?

17:10.571 --> 17:13.573
Taro! Why are you wearing
those raggedy slippers?

17:13.574 --> 17:16.285
How can you even fight in those?

17:17.703 --> 17:22.040
<i>Say your shoes fall off,
or you break a bone.</i>

17:22.041 --> 17:27.004
What makes a fighter truly strong
is being able to adapt to their situation.

17:27.755 --> 17:29.714
But he doesn't get that,

17:29.715 --> 17:33.802
so he recklessly burns through calories
and slims himself down in a wink.

17:41.435 --> 17:42.811
<i>I get it now.</i>

17:44.313 --> 17:47.482
I hit him in the <i>seika tanden</i>
pressure point earlier,

17:47.483 --> 17:54.031
so his body should finally be aware
of how big it actually is.

17:55.365 --> 17:56.450
What?

17:57.451 --> 17:58.535
Where did he...

18:01.038 --> 18:04.291
<i>Once he accepts himself as he really is,</i>

18:04.917 --> 18:09.296
he'll find he has more than enough power
without losing any weight.

18:10.881 --> 18:12.049
How...?

18:13.092 --> 18:15.052
Granny Miya knows best.

18:20.015 --> 18:21.308
<i>Going down.</i>

18:22.101 --> 18:23.685
Time for my counterattack.

18:24.520 --> 18:27.230
Wow, it's so high!
We're going all the way up!

18:27.231 --> 18:29.149
The elevator is see-through!

18:30.400 --> 18:31.652
What's that?

18:39.743 --> 18:41.120
Did something fall?

18:44.123 --> 18:45.541
What's that sound?

18:56.051 --> 18:57.386
This feels good.

18:58.887 --> 19:00.347
Incredible...

19:01.140 --> 19:03.266
This is the longest connection I've had!

19:03.267 --> 19:05.269
You're the first...

19:07.855 --> 19:10.440
This is getting fun.

19:11.024 --> 19:12.276
Will you...

19:13.235 --> 19:16.113
listen to what I have to say?

19:17.281 --> 19:18.532
Sorry.

19:21.410 --> 19:24.246
I don't have the time
to listen to you blabber.

21:01.551 --> 21:05.846
Hey, Osaragi. Suppose we have a bite
at this ramen festival?

21:05.847 --> 21:09.601
But this isn't where
our target is hiding out.

21:10.185 --> 21:11.269
Come off it.

21:11.270 --> 21:13.062
It's like they say, isn't it?

21:13.063 --> 21:15.357
Never go to war on an empty stomach.

21:15.941 --> 21:17.525
Then I want <i>katsudon.</i>

21:17.526 --> 21:20.444
Drop the superstitions for once.

21:20.445 --> 21:23.072
Can't we eat what I want to sometimes?

21:23.073 --> 21:26.909
Besides, noodles are lucky too.

21:26.910 --> 21:31.415
Long noodles symbolize a long life,
which means we won't die on this mission...

21:33.917 --> 21:37.004
Let's go already. I'm hungry.

21:38.213 --> 21:40.506
<i>Talk about doing a 180.</i>

21:40.507 --> 21:42.008
TON TON TEI
IE-KEI TONKOTSU RAMEN

21:42.009 --> 21:44.510
Mr. Shishiba, what is this?

21:44.511 --> 21:47.221
It's pickled ginger, clearly.

21:47.222 --> 21:48.431
Do you eat this too?

21:48.432 --> 21:51.435
It's great for when you want
to change up the flavor later.

21:52.227 --> 21:54.730
You can have mine too.

21:57.274 --> 22:00.318
Osaragi... Let me ask you.

22:00.319 --> 22:02.236
Why did you do that?

22:02.237 --> 22:05.072
You said you wanted it.

22:05.073 --> 22:06.450
I never said that.

22:07.284 --> 22:08.242
You did too.

22:08.243 --> 22:09.410
I did not.

22:09.411 --> 22:12.288
You said it was good
for changing up the flavor.

22:12.289 --> 22:13.956
Now that I did say.

22:13.957 --> 22:15.875
OSHIMA'S
AN AROMATIC WONDERLAND

22:15.876 --> 22:19.587
This is a special type of ramen
topped with cilantro.

22:19.588 --> 22:23.008
Sorry, sir. We've run out of cilantro.

22:25.260 --> 22:27.345
This is my cilantro.

22:29.473 --> 22:30.890
YURURI KICHIJOJI
SPICY NOODLES!

22:30.891 --> 22:33.726
Osaragi, could you pass the spicy sauce?

22:33.727 --> 22:35.770
SPICY - SPICY - GARLIC CHIPS

22:35.771 --> 22:37.189
The red one?

22:40.567 --> 22:42.444
What in the hell is this?!

22:43.487 --> 22:45.196
What's wrong?

22:45.197 --> 22:47.448
Can't you see it says "death" on it?

22:47.449 --> 22:48.950
IPPON SHOBU
AUTHENTIC CHINESE RAMEN

22:49.618 --> 22:51.787
This is the star of the show.

22:52.412 --> 22:56.750
As long as I get to eat this,
I'll have no regrets.

22:57.334 --> 23:00.378
Excuse me. Mind if I sit next to you?

23:01.880 --> 23:03.590
That's the target.

23:04.591 --> 23:06.051
